  "notes": "Warren J. Smith, Modern Lens Design, 2nd ed., Figure 20.6 long, p. 392. Book: EFL 141.6, BFL 101.9, NA -0.0037 (F/133.9), GIH 34.44 (HFOV=13.67), PTZ/F 1.963, VL 38.76, infinite conjugate. Wavelengths 0.6328 um as in the book (primary first). Stop at surface 1 (the book's plane air surface). Zoom lens: lensforge has no multi-configuration support, so each zoom position the book lists is a separate file (short, mid and long). Between positions only the air spaces after surfaces 3, 7, 9 and 11 (the back focus) change. The book lists two dummy plane air surfaces after surface 9, with thicknesses equal to the air spaces after surfaces 3 and 7 (13.278 and 0.972) and sa 0.0, printed without a sign. Only negative values reproduce the book's VL 38.76 and its drawing, so they are folded into the air space after surface 9: 17.973 - 13.278 - 0.972 = 3.723. The stop is the front plane surface (book sa 0.0); its 1.057 diameter follows from the book's EFL and F-number, the same in every position. Book lists sa 0.0 on some surfaces; left as automatic semi-diameter.",
